  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe `increaseTokenBalance()` function in `DistributionCreator.sol` credits users with the full `amount` parameter without verifying the actual tokens received. For fee-on-transfer (FoT) tokens, this creates a permanent accounting mismatch where recorded balances exceed actual contract holdings, leading to protocol insolvency.\n\n## Vulnerability Detail\n\nThe `increaseTokenBalance()` function transfers tokens from the caller and credits the user's balance:\n\n```solidity\nfunction increaseTokenBalance(address user, address rewardToken, uint256 amount) external {\n    if (!accessControlManager.isGovernor(msg.sender))\n        IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n    _updateBalance(user, rewardToken, creatorBalance[user][rewardToken] + amount);\n}\n```\n\nThe issue is that `_updateBalance` credits the full `amount` without measuring how many tokens were actually received. For FoT tokens that deduct a percentage on each transfer, the contract receives fewer tokens than `amount` but credits the full value.\n\nExample with 1% FoT token:\n- User deposits 10,000 tokens\n- Contract receives 9,900 tokens (after 1% fee)\n- User's `creatorBalance` is credited 10,000 tokens\n- 100 token deficit per deposit\n\nAs more users deposit, the deficit accumulates. When users attempt to withdraw via `decreaseTokenBalance()`, the last users will be unable to withdraw their full recorded balance because the contract lacks sufficient tokens.\n\n## Impact\n\n1. Balance Inflation: Recorded balances permanently exceed actual holdings, creating phantom balances.\n\n2. Protocol Insolvency: The contract becomes insolvent - it owes more than it holds.\n\n3. Last Depositor Loss: Users who withdraw later cannot receive their full balance. The deficit is socialized to the last withdrawers.\n\n4. Campaign Funding Failures: Campaigns created using inflated balances will fail or underfund the Distributor contract.\n\nQuantified Impact:\n- With a 1% FoT token and 1,000,000 tokens deposited across users, the protocol has a 10,000 token deficit\n- The last ~1% of withdrawers will be unable to withdraw anything\n- With higher fee tokens (some FoT tokens have 5-10% fees), the impact scales proportionally\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n\nMeasure actual tokens received by checking balance before and after transfer:\n\n```solidity\nfunction increaseTokenBalance(address user, address rewardToken, uint256 amount) external {\n    uint256 actualReceived = amount;\n    if (!accessControlManager.isGovernor(msg.sender)) {\n        uint256 balanceBefore = IERC20(rewardToken).balanceOf(address(this));\n        IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n        actualReceived = IERC20(rewardToken).balanceOf(address(this)) - balanceBefore;\n    }\n    _updateBalance(user, rewardToken, creatorBalance[user][rewardToken] + actualReceived);\n}\n```\n\nAlternatively, explicitly block FoT tokens by validating that the received amount matches the expected amount:\n\n```solidity\nfunction increaseTokenBalance(address user, address rewardToken, uint256 amount) external {\n    if (!accessControlManager.isGovernor(msg.sender)) {\n        uint256 balanceBefore = IERC20(rewardToken).balanceOf(address(this));\n        IERC20(rewardToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n        uint256 actualReceived = IERC20(rewardToken).balanceOf(address(this)) - balanceBefore;\n        if (actualReceived != amount) revert Errors.FeeOnTransferNotSupported();\n    }\n    _updateBalance(user, rewardToken, creatorBalance[user][rewardToken] + amount);\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Add this test to `test/c4/C4PoC.t.sol`:\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\n\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\nimport { ERC20 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\";\n\ncontract FeeOnTransferToken is ERC20 {\n    uint256 public constant FEE_BPS = 100; // 1% fee\n    uint256 public constant BPS_DENOMINATOR = 10000;\n\n    constructor() ERC20(\"FeeOnTransfer\", \"FOT\") {}\n\n    function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external {\n        _mint(to, amount);\n    }\n\n    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) public override returns (bool) {\n        uint256 fee = (amount * FEE_BPS) / BPS_DENOMINATOR;\n        uint256 amountAfterFee = amount - fee;\n        _burn(msg.sender, fee);\n        return super.transfer(to, amountAfterFee);\n    }\n\n    function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amount) public override returns (bool) {\n        uint256 fee = (amount * FEE_BPS) / BPS_DENOMINATOR;\n        uint256 amountAfterFee = amount - fee;\n        _spendAllowance(from, msg.sender, amount);\n        _burn(from, fee);\n        _transfer(from, to, amountAfterFee);\n        return true;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract C4PoC is Fixture {\n    uint256 internal constant maxDistribForOOG = 1e4;\n    uint256 internal constant nbrDistrib = 10;\n    uint32 internal initStartTime;\n    uint32 internal initEndTime;\n    uint32 internal startTime;\n    uint32 internal endTime;\n    uint32 internal numEpoch;\n\n    FeeOnTransferToken fotToken;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        initStartTime = uint32(block.timestamp);\n        numEpoch = 25;\n        initEndTime = startTime + numEpoch * EPOCH_DURATION;\n\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setFeeRecipient(dylan);\n\n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(angle);\n        amounts[0] = 1e8;\n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        angle.mint(address(alice), 1e22);\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n\n        fotToken = new FeeOnTransferToken();\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        uint256 depositAmount = 10000 ether;\n\n        fotToken.mint(alice, depositAmount);\n        fotToken.mint(bob, depositAmount);\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        fotToken.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        fotToken.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        creator.increaseTokenBalance(alice, address(fotToken), depositAmount);\n\n        uint256 aliceRecordedBalance = creator.creatorBalance(alice, address(fotToken));\n        uint256 contractActualBalance = fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator));\n\n        assertEq(aliceRecordedBalance, depositAmount);\n        assertEq(contractActualBalance, 9900 ether);\n\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        creator.increaseTokenBalance(bob, address(fotToken), depositAmount);\n\n        uint256 bobRecordedBalance = creator.creatorBalance(bob, address(fotToken));\n        contractActualBalance = fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator));\n\n        assertEq(bobRecordedBalance, depositAmount);\n        assertEq(contractActualBalance, 19800 ether);\n\n        uint256 totalRecorded = aliceRecordedBalance + bobRecordedBalance;\n        assertEq(totalRecorded, 20000 ether);\n        assertGt(totalRecorded, contractActualBalance);\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        creator.decreaseTokenBalance(alice, address(fotToken), alice, depositAmount);\n\n        contractActualBalance = fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator));\n        assertEq(contractActualBalance, 9800 ether);\n\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        vm.expectRevert(\"ERC20: transfer amount exceeds balance\");\n        creator.decreaseTokenBalance(bob, address(fotToken), bob, depositAmount);\n\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        creator.decreaseTokenBalance(bob, address(fotToken), bob, contractActualBalance);\n\n        uint256 bobFinalBalance = fotToken.balanceOf(bob);\n        assertEq(bobFinalBalance, 9702 ether);\n\n        uint256 bobRemainingRecorded = creator.creatorBalance(bob, address(fotToken));\n        assertEq(bobRemainingRecorded, 200 ether);\n\n        assertEq(fotToken.balanceOf(address(creator)), 0);\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\n\nRun with:\n```bash\nforge test --match-test test_submissionValidity -vvv\n```\n\n\nResult: Bob deposited 10,000 tokens but could only withdraw 9,800. He receives 9,702 after the withdrawal fee. He is left with 200 recorded balance that can never be withdrawn. The contract is empty but still \"owes\" Bob 200 tokens.",
